l engineers.\nM.S. in ME Program\nThe Mechanical Engineering program permits students to deeply explore engineering design and analysis. The interdisciplinary nature of the program provides students with an opportunity to work on exciting research areas at the leading edge of technology.\nPh.D. in Mechanical Engineering Program\nThe Ph.D. in ME Program at Rowan effectively prepares individuals to respond to the changing needs of engineers today. Students will complete higher level coursework in technical topics & will develop and demonstrate applied skills in research, teaching, & communication.\nApplications and Admissions\nAll information about applying to our graduate programs and receiving aid, along with information if you are an international student can be found here.\nSenior Privilege\nSenior Privilege Program is a great option for students considering graduate school after the completion of their undergraduate degree.\nADD (4+1) Program\nThe Accelerated BS/MS Dual Degree Program in ME permits students to complete the 120-credit BS-ME and the 30-credit MS-ME degree (Non-Thesis Option) programs in under five years.\nCertificate of Graduate Studies\nExplore the requirements to complete COGS offered by the ME Department.\nMechanical Engineering\nBack to Mechanical Engineering (ME)\nMain Menu\nMechanical Engineering (ME)\nAbout Us\nProgram Goals & Objectives\nDepartmental Contacts\nCampus Map & Directions\nAccreditation\nExternal Advisory Board\nTrends & Statistics\nHonors & Awards\nUndergraduate Programs\nB.S. in ME Curriculum\nMinors\nCertificate of Undergraduate Studies\nSummer Courses\nCo-op Programs\nGraduate Programs\nM.S. in ME Program\nPh.D. in ME Program\nSenior Privilege\nADD (4+1) Program\nCertificate of Graduate Studies\nFaculty & Staff\nSupporting Faculty\nAdvising and FAQ\nStudent Resources\nHelpful Links\nProfessional Societies\nPurchase Request\nStudent Clubs\nProspective Students\nEngineering Clinic\nResearch\nNews\nME News\nCollege of Engineeri